`reconstruction_error` converts a list or a DataFrame to an array, so it returns an array instead of failing or returning a DataFrame or Series. `TrajectoryResult` and `TrajectoryResult.from_grid` raise when `times` does not have one entry per time point, which used to give wrong speeds and AUCs silently. `trajectory_curvature(method="cosine")` is NaN where a step has zero length: its direction is undefined, and it used to read as a right angle divided by machine epsilon (about 7e15 for one repeated point).
